  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member on a slow network, I want a second composer action to be refused while the first is still fetching its form, so that one page never ends with two composers set (LESSONS 11: a guard covers every path that acts).\n\n### Scenario\nTap \"+ › Editer\" on a slow network, then \"Répondre\" while \"Chargement de l'édition…\" shows. The reply composer opens; when the prefill arrives, `editor` is set too. Symmetric: \"Citer\" in flight, then \"Editer\".\n\n### Evidence (`7a61018f`)\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/Actions/MessageWriteModel.swift:62-68`: `guard progress == nil, editor == nil`, then `try await services.poster.editPrefill(target)`, then `editor = ReplyComposerModel(editing: …)` with no check of the reader after the await.\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/Quote/TopicReaderModel+Quote.swift:23-24`: `requestReply` checks `suspendsPageInteractions` only before its own awaits.\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/ReaderPageControls.swift:194-197`: the reply button is disabled by `isLoadingQuote || suspendsPageInteractions`, not by `writes.progress`.\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/TopicReaderModel+Composer.swift:196`: `suspendsPageInteractions` is true only once a composer is presented.\n\n### Fix\nOne \"busy\" notion on the reader, set before the first await of `openEditor`, `requestReply`, `quoteMessage` and `quoteSelection`; re-check after each await and drop the late result with a feedback line.\n\n### Test (fails before the fix)\n`MessageWriteModelTests.aReplyOpenedDuringAnEditPrefillKeepsOneComposer`: poster suspended in `editPrefill`, `reader.requestReply()` opens the reply composer, resume the prefill, `writes.editor == nil`.\n\nConfidence: high on the state (two composers set); the visible result (second sheet queued or refused by SwiftUI) was not observed.\n\nRework model: Sonnet 5.5, reviewed by Opus 5.5.\n\nFound by #775 (cloud/r775-fable, Fable 5.2). Reviewed at `dev-swift` @ `7a61018f`; read from the code, not run on a device unless stated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
